    "finding": "The identical original SKP replays with zero RGBA error on macOS Chromium, while CanvasKit has deterministic text-region errors. Record contents, layout and transport are intact for this case; the mismatch is in client font raster behavior.",
    "backendContext": "macOS Skia uses CoreText; the software CanvasKit build uses FreeType. Existing extra stem-darkening calibration targets CFF, while the CERN fonts are TrueType. Exact remaining per-glyph raster parameter attribution is not yet complete.",
    "scope": "Native macOS raster was used only as a separate diagnostic control; those PNGs never enter production native frame delivery. White-background composition follows the captured frame background. CSS smoothing ablations are not replacement acceptance references.",
    "fixDirection": "Match the client/server font raster policy or use a matching native replay backend. A single smoothing CSS switch did not pass all original pixel limits; limits remain unchanged.",
    "limits": {
      "maxMeanAbsoluteChannelError": 3,
      "maxPixelsOver32Fraction": 0.02,
      "significantChannelDelta": 32
    }
  },
